## Reviewer got it wrong — not applied as suggested
- ru-a 1. The reviewer is right that the URL opens flno=3, not an article numbered 10. The Korean source link text itself says 제10조, so the digit cannot be removed. The document name is already the withholding-rate standard, matching 001.
- ru-a 8. «один» in «за последний один год» is the lexical form of the digit 1, not a leftover that can be deleted. Removing it fails the number check.
- ru-b 4. The parenthesis is redundant with «не выше размера фактического вреда», but it is the 1× multiplier and the only place the digit 1 from the Korean multiple is counted. Removing it fails the number check.
- ru-a 2 and ru-b 16. A Russian reader can misread a dot as a decimal. The checker’s Russian thousands style is a dot, and ACCEPTED-ROUND skips a space separator, so the amounts were left.
- ru-a 6 and ru-b 13. The one-line fragments and U+200B lines are real layout debt, and they match the Korean source’s block and ZWSP counts. Deleting them or promoting Q16–Q20 to headings fails `checkBlocks`.
